1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,688
An A.I.

2
00:00:01,688 --> 00:00:05,448
voice agent can answer the calls to one of your numbers, find out

3
00:00:05,448 --> 00:00:09,048
why people are calling, and hand them to a person when needed.

4
00:00:09,048 --> 00:00:12,701
This video shows how to route a number to it, what happens when

5
00:00:12,701 --> 00:00:16,725
you are open and closed, the subject that gives it outcomes, and where

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,102
you review the call.

7
00:00:18,102 --> 00:00:22,020
Calls never connect on this demo site, so the live parts use slides.

8
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:30,003
A call to a number reaches an inbound entry point.

9
00:00:30,003 --> 00:00:33,929
An entry point can send it to a queue, to a specific agent,

10
00:00:33,929 --> 00:00:35,077
or to an A.I.

11
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:36,164
voice agent.

12
00:00:36,164 --> 00:00:37,312
With the A.I.

13
00:00:37,312 --> 00:00:42,145
voice agent, the caller skips the welcome message, the menu and the queue,

14
00:00:42,145 --> 00:00:44,380
and talks to the agent at once.

15
00:00:45,130 --> 00:00:47,208
This works with Telnyx only.

16
00:00:47,208 --> 00:00:51,853
If the call arrives on the Asterisk provider, it cannot be answered by

17
00:00:51,853 --> 00:00:54,420
the agent, and the call is rejected.

18
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:56,730
The agent is an A.I.

19
00:00:56,730 --> 00:00:58,470
profile that you write:

20
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:02,070
what to ask, what it may answer, and when to transfer.

21
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:07,650
The call becomes an automated activity, so you can review it afterwards like any other.

22
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:14,551
Open Inbound entry points, and click Add.

23
00:01:14,551 --> 00:01:15,999
Choose Voice calls.

24
00:01:15,999 --> 00:01:20,227
Name the entry point, and pick the number it answers under Numbers.

25
00:01:20,227 --> 00:01:24,860
The numbers come from Omnichannel Addresses that are used for voice calls.

26
00:01:25,313 --> 00:01:28,141
On Routing, Route to has three choices:

27
00:01:28,141 --> 00:01:30,467
Queue, Specific agent, and A.I.

28
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,598
voice agent.

29
00:01:31,598 --> 00:01:36,123
The last one appears when the Telnyx AI Voice Agent feature is on.

30
00:01:36,123 --> 00:01:37,946
Choose it, and the A.I.

31
00:01:37,946 --> 00:01:39,643
agent picker appears.

32
00:01:40,096 --> 00:01:42,566
The picker lists your chat profiles.

33
00:01:42,566 --> 00:01:47,505
Saving without one is refused, with a message that asks you to select the A.I.

34
00:01:47,505 --> 00:01:50,446
agent that answers this entry point's calls.

35
00:01:50,446 --> 00:01:52,386
Pick the profile, and save.

36
00:01:56,593 --> 00:02:01,509
On Hours, the Business hours calendar decides when the entry point is open.

37
00:02:01,509 --> 00:02:03,451
While it is open, the A.I.

38
00:02:03,451 --> 00:02:05,333
agent answers every call.

39
00:02:05,786 --> 00:02:09,903
Closed action decides what happens outside the hours:

40
00:02:09,903 --> 00:02:13,462
Hold in queue, Voicemail, Overflow or Reject.

41
00:02:13,462 --> 00:02:14,369
An A.I.

42
00:02:14,369 --> 00:02:19,882
entry point has no queue, so Hold in queue and Overflow act as Voicemail.

43
00:02:19,882 --> 00:02:21,696
Reject stays reject.

44
00:02:22,182 --> 00:02:23,739
On Voicemail, an A.I.

45
00:02:23,739 --> 00:02:28,759
entry point should deliver to An agent's inbox, and you pick the Voicemail inbox.

46
00:02:28,759 --> 00:02:32,625
The queue's shared voicemail box needs a queue, which an A.I.

47
00:02:32,625 --> 00:02:34,472
entry point does not have.

48
00:02:38,713 --> 00:02:42,371
The call needs an inbound subject to get outcomes.

49
00:02:42,371 --> 00:02:45,050
Open an inbound subject's settings.

50
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:51,779
Direction is Inbound, Interaction type is Automated, Channel is Phone, and Address is the number.

51
00:02:51,779 --> 00:02:55,373
A call is matched to its subject by that address.

52
00:02:55,849 --> 00:02:56,672
The A.I.

53
00:02:56,672 --> 00:02:58,964
configuration card holds the A.I.

54
00:02:58,964 --> 00:03:02,314
profile, the Subject goal, and the speech settings.

55
00:03:02,314 --> 00:03:07,897
The profile list shows only profiles with Start the conversation automatically turned on.

56
00:03:07,897 --> 00:03:12,069
The goal tells the agent when to disposition the call and end it.

57
00:03:12,593 --> 00:03:17,456
Live agent handoff lets the agent transfer to a person, into the Handoff

58
00:03:17,456 --> 00:03:20,511
queue you choose, for the reasons you tick.

59
00:03:20,511 --> 00:03:24,813
Without a subject, the call has no dispositions and no handoff.

60
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:33,122
A call can be turn-based, or a live audio conversation.

61
00:03:33,122 --> 00:03:37,739
Turn-based, each turn is spoken and transcribed through Telnyx.

62
00:03:37,739 --> 00:03:43,494
A live conversation needs the Contact Center Voice Media feature, and a realtime

63
00:03:43,494 --> 00:03:47,710
deployment, so the model speaks and listens continuously.

64
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:51,351
Do not mix up two things with the same name.

65
00:03:51,351 --> 00:03:55,555
Contact Center Voice Media is the feature for two-way audio.

66
00:03:55,555 --> 00:04:01,796
Voice Media, under Interaction Center, Management, is the library of hold music and prompts.

67
00:04:01,796 --> 00:04:04,726
It is part of the Contact Center itself.

68
00:04:08,926 --> 00:04:14,083
If recording is announced to inbound callers, the notice is spoken first.

69
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:15,910
Then the agent greets.

70
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:19,696
Turn-based, it speaks the profile's opening message.

71
00:04:19,696 --> 00:04:25,896
In a live conversation, the model words its own greeting from the profile's instructions.

72
00:04:26,646 --> 00:04:30,650
A caller who says nothing is never mistaken for a voicemail.

73
00:04:30,650 --> 00:04:35,866
The agent asks if they are there, and ends the call politely if they stay quiet.

74
00:04:36,616 --> 00:04:40,609
When a reason you ticked applies, the call goes to the handoff queue.

75
00:04:40,609 --> 00:04:44,656
The agent who answers sees a summary written by the A.I., labeled A.I.

76
00:04:44,656 --> 00:04:48,276
assistant's summary, so the caller does not repeat everything.

77
00:04:52,535 --> 00:04:53,293
An A.I.

78
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:57,721
call is logged as an activity of the subject, with the disposition the

79
00:04:57,721 --> 00:05:00,342
agent chose and a summary in the notes.

80
00:05:00,342 --> 00:05:02,498
Dispositioned by shows the A.I.

81
00:05:02,498 --> 00:05:04,479
voice agent and its profile.

82
00:05:04,479 --> 00:05:06,285
The call here is made up.

83
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,778
Review A.I.

84
00:05:07,778 --> 00:05:10,891
conversation opens the transcript, read only.

85
00:05:10,891 --> 00:05:13,883
The Call recordings page also lists an A.I.

86
00:05:13,883 --> 00:05:17,730
recording with its transcript, when call recording is on.

87
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:24,508
A front desk that never misses a call:

88
00:05:24,508 --> 00:05:29,548
the agent answers, takes a message or answers simple questions, and transfers to

89
00:05:29,548 --> 00:05:32,010
your team when someone is available.

90
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,356
A line for busy seasons:

91
00:05:34,356 --> 00:05:36,803
point the number you promote at the A.I.

92
00:05:36,803 --> 00:05:41,060
voice agent, so the wait does not depend on how many agents are signed in.

93
00:05:41,810 --> 00:05:43,218
After-hours triage:

94
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:47,500
collect the reason for the call, and book a follow-up for the morning.

95
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,345
Route a number to an A.I.

96
00:05:51,345 --> 00:05:57,002
voice agent, give it a subject for outcomes and handoff, and review each call afterwards.

97
00:05:57,002 --> 00:05:58,550
Thanks for watching.

